Corresponding source
--------------------
The published files of a release (sidecar-<version>.elemod, the companion;
rytm-sidecar-<version>.elemod; and core-0.9-os1.74.elemod beside them) are
built from this repository at the release's tag, v<version>:
`make setup`, then `make release` (docs/ELEKLOADER.md), with the toolchain
the release's TOOLCHAIN.txt names (the bytes depend on the m68k-elf-as
version, and the core's on the m68k-linux-gnu-gcc version). That tag holds
the complete source of our bytes (mods/, registry/, re/, tools/) and pins the
exact third-party sources the build uses (Makefile, tools/build.py):

  - core-0.9-os1.74.elemod is elekloader's core-ar2 0.9 for OS 1.74, built
    unchanged by elekloader's own builder from mods/core-ar2 and mods/core
    at elekloader commit 9f72fb05bd3baeacdf04af00dc2d1357abf96134
    (https://github.com/irpina/elekloader, GPL-2.0-or-later);
  - the builder, linker and packer are elekloader at the same commit;
  - since 2026-11-05 the companion (sidecar-<version>.elemod) is built from
    its own repository, sidecar-core, at the commit the Makefile pins
    (SC_REV, cloned to vendor/sidecar-core by `make setup`). A release must
    publish that source too (the repository, or an archive of it beside the
    files), which `make release` does not do yet.

Their source is also in the release folder, beside the files (GPL-2.0
section 3): elekloader-9f72fb0-src.tar.gz (all of elekloader at 9f72fb0,
with its LICENSE and NOTICE).

Some of our stubs are generated from C (mods/*/build.sh says how); the C file
is the source, the generated stub.s is committed beside it.

Third-party code
----------------
Nothing below is copied into this repository. `make setup` fetches it into
vendor/ (git-ignored) at pinned commits, and the build executes it.

  vendor/elekloader
      https://github.com/irpina/elekloader, (C) 2026 irpina and contributors,
      GPL-2.0-or-later (its LICENSE and NOTICE; its js/ kit, not used here, is
      GPL-3.0-or-later). Builds the elemods, links them into the image
      with its core-ar2 (boot copier and hook bus), packs and checks the .syx.
      A built image, and core-0.1-os1.74.elemod, contain elekloader's core-ar2 code.

  vendor/elektron-firmware-tool
      https://github.com/mischa85/elektron-firmware-tool, (C) 2026 Marcel
      Bierling, MIT licence (its LICENSE). Unpacks and repacks the .syx
      container; our checks extract every image with it.

  mods/0033-plaits/blob/vendor/eurorack
      https://github.com/pichenettes/eurorack (Plaits and stmlib), (C) Emilie
      Gillet, MIT licence (the notice in each source file). Fetched by
      mods/0033-plaits/blob/build.sh at 08460a6 (stmlib e3bd7c9) and compiled
      into the PLAITS blob, which a build carries as 0033-plaits's payload:
      a built image with 0033 contains Plaits' code, under its MIT notice.

